Table 2.2: Basic parameters for the RHICBefore ion beams are injected into the RHIC rings, the ions are pre-accelerated and bunched. The injectors consist of three accelerators, the Alternating Gradient Synchrotron (AGS), the Booster synchrotron and Tandem Van de Graaff accelerators. The layout for the RHIC collider and injectors are shown in Fig. 2.1.

The gold ions emitted from ion source are initially with charge -1 and accelerated by Tandem Van de Graaff. At the middle of Tandem Van de Graaff the ions pass gold foils and are positively ionized to charge +14. The ions with kinetic energy of 1 MeV/u are transferred to the Booster synchrotron to be accelerated to 72 MeV/u. At the end of the Booster acceleration these ions

Figure 2.1: Layout of the RHIC complex

are further stripped to be charged to +77 and the ion beams are contracted as bunches and enter the AGS. The AGS accelerates the ions to the kinetic energy of 10.8 GeV/u. Then the last two electrons are finally stripped and the ions are to be charged to +79. These ion bunches are injected to the RHIC and accelerated to the full RHIC energy.

