The event-wise two-point temperature distribution \(\tau_{2}(\beta_{1},\beta_{2};\beta_{0},n^{\prime}(\Delta e))\) may be expressed as a combination of uncorrelated and correlated two-point temperature distributions. The former, \(\tau_{2,uncorr}\), is expressed as a simple product of the single-particle event-internal temperature distributions according to a factorization assumption,

