## Chapter 6 Two-particle Transverse-Moment Correlations

Results from two-particle transverse momentum correlation analysis of Au-Au collisions at 130 GeV per nucleon pair are presented in this chapter. Results are divided into charge-independent (CI) and charge-dependent (CD) parts of correlation structures. Observations of substantial nonstatistical fluctuations in event-wise mean transverse momentum \(<p_{t}>\) of charged particles (CI) [41, 75, 76] and charge dependent (CD) part of fluctuations [41] from Au-Au collisions at RHIC energies (\(\sqrt{s_{NN}}=130\), 200 GeV) suggest corresponding correlation structures in transverse-momentum two-particle space.

