The fixed-scale (full-acceptance) correlation measurement of saddle curvatures could set a lower limit on global temperature fluctuation of \(\sigma_{T}/T_{0}\geq\sqrt{\Delta(1/n)_{tot}/2}\sim 1\%\) for central events. Upper limit \(\sigma_{T}/T_{0}\leq\sqrt{1/n}\sim 30\%\) is derived from the inclusive \(p_{t}\) distribution.

