transverse two-particle density ratio and the minimum standard errors are \(0.8\times 10^{-4}\), \(0.8\times 10^{-4}\), \(2.2\times 10^{-4}\) and \(6.0\times 10^{-4}\) near center (\(x(p_{t1})\sim x(p_{t2})\simeq 0.5\)) for CI correlation space. The standard errors for CD correlation are about twice of the error sizes in CI correlation space.

#### Charge Symmetry

Study of CI and CD two-particle correlation structures by combining and subtracting LS and US distributions presupposes charge symmetry of correlations, _i.e._, invariance of correlation structure under exchange of charge sign of particles in each LS and US two-particle density ratio. The assumption of charge-symmetry is confirmed in this section.

Transverse two-particle density ratio of each LS and US charge combinations are shown in Fig. 6.16 (i) and (ii). The right-hand panels represent the difference distributions of the two-particle density ratio of each charge sign combinations. The bottom plots (iii, iv) are bin-number distributions of differences. Small correlation structure on the difference distribution plots and the bin-number histograms which agree with statistical distribution show that the charge-combination symmetry is achieved in both LS and US transverse two-particle correlations.

