Motivated by an approximate independence of correlation structures of the axial-momentum sums \(\phi_{\Sigma}\equiv\phi_{1}+\phi_{2}\) and \(\eta_{\Sigma}\equiv\eta_{1}+\eta_{2}\), we obtain projections of two-particle density ratios onto the difference (\(\phi_{\Delta}\equiv\phi_{1}-\phi_{2}\), \(\eta_{\Delta}\equiv\eta_{1}-\eta_{2}\)) diagonals to create one-dimensional autocorrelations (Sec. 3.2) without loss

