#### Mixed-Event Selections

The mixed-pair reference distributions are constructed from the pairs taken from different events of close properties as described in Sec. 5.5. Construction of mixed-pairs from events of insufficient close properties leads undesirable effects [70]. Appropriateness of the mixed-event selections are tested by comparing joint autocorrelations constructed from different mixed-pair selections of multiplicity difference and vertex position along beam-axis difference.

In Fig. 7.17, the CD (i, ii) and CI (iii, iv) axial joint autocorrelation formed with different selections of mixed-pair construction are presented. The results with the mixed-pair distributions used in this study (left-hand panels) and with the tighten selection (middle panels) and the two-dimensional difference are presented in the right-hand panels. The different selections are shown as black and red points in Fig. 5.8. Small structure on the difference plots confirms that the conditions used in this analysis are sufficient and effects from mixed-pair distributions are negligible.

#### Total Systematic Error

Total systematic error on the axial two-particle correlation space is obtained by adding the preceding non-negligible errors of each bin quadratically.

